\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria \highlight\uc2 's naira rallies for second day on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2014\par 15:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Naira down 11.8 percent this year as oil price drops (Adds naira close, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , comment from dealers)\par \par \uc2 By Chijioke Ohuocha and Oludare Mayowa\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Dec 3 (Reuters) - Nigeria's naira rose for the second straight day on Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars but still closed below the bottom of its new target range, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The naira has lost 11.8 percent against the dollar this year, as global oil prices plunged, worsening the already shaky finances of Africa's top oil producing nation.\par \par \uc2 The naira ended up about 0.6 percent at 179.90 against the dollar from Tuesday's close of 181 naira. It firmed almost four percent on the previous day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up from another record intraday low.\par \par \uc2 The naira was hovering around 183.15 naira to the dollar for almost three hours before Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shown commitment to support the naira, but reserves are going down and at the end of the day the bank's ability to sustain its support will be hampered," a dealer said.\par \par \uc2 "We expect more drastic measures in the near term," he said.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's foreign reserves fell to a six-month low of $36.7 billion by Dec. 1, down 4.5 percent from the previous month, limiting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to keep defending the naira.\par \par \uc2 The bank devalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 8 percent last week in a bid to halt a decline in foreign reserves but it has been struggling to keep the naira within its new band of 160-176 to the dollar. (Editing by Louise Ireland) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-3T15:15:50.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141203eac300llu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
