\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria \highlight\uc2 's naira spikes higher after  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2014\par 15:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Naira gains 1.7 pct on the dollar from previous close\par \par \uc2 * Market expects large dollar sales from state oil company (Adds dollar sales, naira close, dealers)\par \par \uc2 By Chijioke Ohuocha and Oludare Mayowa\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Dec 2 (Reuters) - Nigeria's naira rose sharply against the dollar on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times to lift it from yet another record intraday low, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The naira closed at 181 against the dollar, up 3.6 percent from its early session low of 187.55 naira. The unit closed at 184.10 the previous day.\par \par \uc2 As oil prices stay persistenly weak around five-year lows, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which devalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 8 percent last week, has been struggling to keep the naira trading within its new band of 160-176 naira to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The naira has lost 12.3 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said oil companies were also selling dollars and some banks were buying naira ahead of a Wednesday's Treasury bill auction.\par \par \uc2 China's Addax sold $4.5 million, while \uc2 Mobil\uc2 's $36 million and \uc2 Saipem\uc2 's $15 million Monday sales hit the market on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the naira to strengthen further ... if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  this way ... coupled with the market expecting large dollar sales from (state-owned oil company) NNPC," one dealer said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to meet dollar demand at its twice-weekly auction the previous day when it sold about $169 million dollars at 168 naira versus last week's rate of 165 naira, dealers said. The bank has typically sold between about $200 million and $300 million at previous auctions.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  devalued the naira last Tuesday to try to halt a decline in the foreign reserves of Africa's leading energy producer as oil prices slump. Reserves are down to $36.8 billion by Nov. 28, compared with $44.6 billion a year ago.\par \par \uc2 But doubts remain about whether the devaluation went far enough given the likelihood of continuing low oil prices and the bank's inability to maintain the new band.\par \par \uc2 Brent oil was trading below $72 a barrel. (Editing by Louise Ireland) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-2T15:21:09.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141202eac200dnp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
