\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to prop up naira - dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2014\par 15:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background)\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Nov 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market with dollar sales on Thursday to try to keep the naira within a preferred band since it was devalued two days earlier, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The local unit closed up 1.4 percent at 174.30 to the dollar in volatile trade.\par \par \uc2 It had earlier lost around 0.33 percent in intraday trading, breaching the lower end of the bank's target band of 5 percent plus or minus 168.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touched a record low against the dollar on Wednesday, a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  devalued it by 8 percent in a move thought likely to complicate efforts to contain inflation in Africa's biggest economy.\par \par \uc2 The bank's decision to devalue, less than three months before a presidential election, was praised by economists as a bold move, but there remains a debate about whether or not it went far enough.\par \par \uc2 Africa's leading energy producer is contending with a 30 percent fall in world oil prices since June and has spent billions of dollars of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves trying to defend the naira at what markets perceived to be an unrealistic level.\par \par \uc2 According to its website, \uc2 Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent an average of $27.9 million a day this year defending the naira, but it has still shed 11 percent over the same time period.\par \par \uc2 The coming weeks will test its ability to maintain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its new target band. (Reporting by Oludare Mayowa; Writing by Tim Cocks; Editing by Julia Payne)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-30T14:00:12.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141127eabr00ent\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
