\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Nov 18\b0\par\par\uc2 605 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2014\par 05:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, Nov 18 (Reuters) - - The following company announcements, scheduled economic\par indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on\par Tuesday.\par     - - - - -\par  EVENTS:\par  SOUTH AFRICA - \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  auctions 2.35 billion rand of its\par  2032           , 2037            and 2048            bonds.\par  SOUTH AFRICA - Cement maker PPC          is due to issue\par  results. \par  BOTSWANA - \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Botswana\f28 \uc2 \f2  may announce latest decision on\par  benchmark lending rate             .\par  GHANA - South Africa's \f28 \uc2 \f2 AngloGold Ashanti\f28 \uc2 \f2           holds a\par  news conference in Accra.\par  \par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  Japanese shares led a tentative recovery in Asian markets on\par  Tuesday, drawing some support from two U.S. blockbuster\par  acquisitions and anticipation of more European monetary\par  stimulus.            \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par  Brent crude         slipped below $79 a barrel on Tuesday,\par  headed for its sixth daily fall in seven, as oil prices\par  struggle to find a floor ahead of next week's critical \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  meeting.      \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par             \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par  * South Africa's rand          weakened against the dollar\par  Monday as markets braced for consumer inflation numbers and\par  an interest rate decision by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  later in the\par  week.                \par  * South African stocks          edged lower on Monday, as\par  sharp losses in construction and engineering firm Group Five\par           were offset by a strong performance by gold\par  producers taking advantage of better bullion prices.\par                 \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  Kenya's shilling        held firm against the dollar on\par  Monday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the end of last\par  week by selling dollars, lifting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from\par  three-year lows, while stocks closed lower.                \par  \par  NIGERIA MARKETS\par  Nigeria's naira          closed at a new low of 173.20\par  against the dollar on Monday, down 1.21 percent from the\par  previous session even though the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par  prop up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.                \par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 NIGERIA FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  Nigeria's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves             fell 3\par  percent in two weeks to $37.59 billion by Nov. 13, as the\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped up support for the ailing naira\par           \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .                \par  \par  NIGERIA INSURGENCY\par  Nigerian President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goodluck Jonathan\f28 \uc2 \f2  will ask the national\par  assembly to extend a state of emergency in three\par  northeastern states hit by an Islamist insurgency when it\par  expires this week, the justice minister said on Monday.\par                 \par  \par  ZIMBABWE BONDS\par  A state-owned Zimbabwean bank will float two bonds worth $65\par  million on Tuesday to boost electricity output and increase\par  use of pre-paid meters, a senior bank official said.\par                    \par  \par  IVORY COAST AIRLINE   \par  Ivory Coast's national carrier Air Cote d'Ivoire has picked\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Airbus\f28 \uc2 \f2           to renew and expand its fleet after talks\par  last month with the European planemaker and Canada's\par  Bombardier          , the company's chief executive said on\par  Monday.               \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA DRUGS\par  South Africa plans to spend $2.2 billion over two years to\par  buy HIV/AIDS drugs for public hospitals, a government\par  minister said on Monday, as a study shows the prevalence of\par  the virus is rising.                \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA RETAILER    \par  South African retailer Mr Price          reported a 23\par  percent jump in first-half earnings on Monday, as its focus\par  on budget-conscious shoppers and cash sales helped it ride\par  out weak retail and consumer credit markets.                \par  \par  KENYA COURT CASE\par  Kenya's High Court said on Monday the government's\par  anti-graft agency and chief prosecutor could pursue an abuse\par  of office case against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief, and his\par  lawyer had been granted two weeks to appeal the decision.\par                 \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-18T05:25:59.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141118eabi003pi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
