\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Nov 7\b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2014\par 06:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, Nov 7 (Reuters) - - The following company announcements, scheduled economic\par indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on\par Friday.\par     - - - - -\par  EVENTS:\par  MAURITIUS- Inflation data due to be released\par  SEYCHELLES - Inflation data due to be released\par  \par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  Asian shares edged down on Friday ahead of U.S. employment\par  data later in the session, while the euro wallowed around\par  two-year lows after European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Mario\par  Draghi vowed to take more easing steps to spark growth in\par  the euro zone.            \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par  Brent crude dropped for the second straight session on\par  Friday, dragged below $83 by worries over the strong U.S.\par  dollar.      \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par             \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on      \par  \par  AFRICAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  Agricultural inflows and a slowdown in demand for dollars in\par  Tanzania should keep the shilling in familiar ranges next\par  week, while worry about the implications of Zambian\par  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michael Sata\f28 \uc2 \f2 's death is expected to weigh on the\par  kwacha.               \par  \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICAN MARKETS\par  * South African stocks slipped on Thursday with retailers\par  hit after Truworths          reported slower sales,\par  increasing investor concern about the health of\par  cash-strapped consumers.                \par  * The South African rand traded near a three-week low\par  against the dollar late on Thursday, reflecting lukewarm\par  demand for emerging-market assets as the global economic\par  outlook worsens.                \par  \par  NIGERIA MARKETS\par  Nigeria's naira fell 3 percent to a new intraday low on\par  Thursday of 172 to the dollar, recovering ground to close at\par  169.50 only after a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aimed at\par  halting its slide.                \par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 NIGERIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ECONOMY\par  A sharp drop in global oil prices has raised the twin\par  spectres of a potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devaluation and budget\par  shortfalls in Nigeria just as Africa's biggest economy gears\par  up for a closely fought and costly presidential election in\par  February.                \par  \par  NIGERIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 Nigeria's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  banned the sale of dollars to\par  importers of telecom equipment, power generators and\par  finished products at its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  auction, instead\par  shifting demand to the interbank market, dealers told\par  Reuters on Thursday.                        \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS     \par  The Kenyan shilling        hovered at a near three-year low\par  on Thursday, with traders saying it was likely to remain on\par  the strong side of 89.90 due to chances of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at that level.                \par  \par  UGANDA OIL\par  Uganda will sign oil production licences with France's Total\par  TOTF.PA and Britain's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tullow Oil\f28 \uc2 \f2  TLW.L by the end of the\par  year as it seeks to start commercial production by 2018, the\par  energy minister said on Thursday.                        \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-7T06:55:47.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141107eab70063j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
