\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Nigerian markets fall,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  as weak oil price pressures naira\b0\par\par\uc2 541 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2014\par 16:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Foreign investors exit \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets on naira concerns\par \par \uc2 * Main stock index down 1.6 pct at 36,744 points\par \par \uc2 * Stocks down 9.6 pct this year as investors exit\par \par \uc2 * Naira down 4.3 pct in 2014, unnerved by falling oil price (Adds closing values, quote, cenbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 By Oludare Mayowa and Chijioke Ohuocha\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Nov 4 (Reuters) - Nigeria's main share index hit a 13-month low and government bonds fell on Tuesday as foreign investors pulled out of Nigerian assets, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars to support the ailing naira.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come under pressure in the past two months from falling global oil prices, dampening appetite for assets in Africa's biggest economy and chief oil exporter.\par \par \uc2 Though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year to prop up its value, the naira has lost 4.3 percent since Jan. 2.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors pulled more money out of the stock market on Tuesday, mainly in the relatively liquid banking and cement sectors, as the oil price fell 3 percent to a four-year low of just above $82 a barrel and as Nigerian companies reported mixed results.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's main share index closed down 1.6 percent at 36,744 points, a level last seen on Oct. 7, 2013. The index has now fallen 11 percent in the past month, although it picked up briefly last week.\par \par \uc2 The naira, which had earlier lost 0.3 percent intraday against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as funds repatriated cash, recovered some ground after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to close down 0.1 percent at 165.90 to the dollar, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "Stocks failed to sustain the recovery recorded in the previous week ... as companies posted mixed performance in the third quarter," one stockbroker told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Dangote Cement\uc2 , sub-Saharan Africa's leading cement producer and majority owned by billionaire Aliko Dangote, reported just a 1.5 percent rise in pretax profit in the nine months to September.\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 Dangote Cement\uc2 , which accounts for a third of the stock market's total capitalisation and whose outlook is linked to the overall state of the economy, dropped 1.7 percent, dragging down the index.\par \par \uc2 Concerns about the naira amid falling global oil prices also triggered a drop in bond prices as investors demand higher returns to hold Nigerian bonds.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the benchmark 10-year bond rose 7 basis point to 12.70 percent on Tuesday, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Two dealers told Reuters that the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had seen strong demand for dollars amid tight supply from offshore investors selling assets and repatriating funds.\par \par \uc2 The local unit of Italian oil firm Eni sold $25 million alongside the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the naira.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's stock market rose 47 percent last year, vastly outperforming emerging market peers which were down on average 4.9 percent.\par \par \uc2 But this year Nigeria's stock index is down 9.6 percent.\par \par \uc2 Other top decliners on Tuesday included cement giant \uc2 Lafarge Africa\uc2  and its listed local subsidiary \uc2 Ashaka Cement\uc2  , whose shares both dropped 5 percent. (Editing by David Holmes and Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-7T15:36:08.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141104eab4009ye\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
