\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria \highlight\uc2  naira closes at 7-month low, despite cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2014\par 17:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Stocks at 1-month low as funds exit\par \par \uc2 * Benchmark 10-year bond down 27 basis point\par \par \uc2 * Oil price worry investors holding Nigerian assets (Adds quote, closing naira value, equity and bond index)\par \par \uc2 By Chijioke Ohuocha and Oludare Mayowa\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Nigeria's naira \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased to a 7-month closing low against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday, despite a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop it up, as falling oil prices pushed investors out of domestic debt and equity markets, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The unit closed at 164.50 naira to the dollar, a level last seen on March 6, but down just 0.1 percent from the 164.35 naira it closed at on Friday. Financial markets were closed on Monday and Tuesday to mark a two-day Muslim holiday.\par \par \uc2 The naira had slipped to 165.30 intraday, which prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in with an undisclosed amount of dollars to try to satisfy demand.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come under pressure in the past two months from falling global oil prices, dampening appetite for assets in Africa's biggest economy. Though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  since this year to prop up its value, it has lost 3.5 percent since January 2.\par \par \uc2 The local unit of China's Addax petroleum also sold around $3 million on Wednesday, which was not sufficient to support the naira, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said yield on the 10-year benchmark bond rose 27 basis points to 12.80 percent on Wednesday while the all-share index fell to a one-month closing low of 40,995 points, down 0.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil fell to a fresh 27-month low under $91 a barrel on Wednesday, as gloomy economic growth forecasts prompted concerns about global oil demand and U.S. inventory data confirmed abundant supply. (Editing by Tim Cocks)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-11T15:31:53.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141008eaa800ilh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
