\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria \highlight\uc2  naira gains 0.15 pct on  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2014\par 18:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (details, quote)\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The Nigerian naira gained 0.15 percent against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which weakened during midday trade on strong demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The unit closed at 162.70 naira to the greenback, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold an undisclosed amount of dollars to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which weakened to 163.85 naira intraday. The naira closed at 162.95 against the dollar on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "Some banks that got (dollars) from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are selling to stay within their open limit position," one dealer said, adding that the regulator sold hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to lenders to calm the volatile naira market.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the naira could come under pressure if there's a fall in the price of crude oil hovering at around $99 a barrel. Crude makes up around 95 percent of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings.\par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll sees Brent crude oil capped around $105.30 a barrel next year, which bodes well for Nigeria's revenues. But an increase in supply of shale oil from the United States and sluggish global demand may mean that is as high as the oil price will go.\par \par \uc2 The naira fell to a 2-month low of 162.87 against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, as dollar sales by the government-owned oil company, NNPC failed to meet market expectations. (Reporting by Chijioke Ohuocha and Oludare Mayowa; Editing by Tim Cocks) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-9-16T17:33:08.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140916ea9g00i5u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
