\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Aug 4\b0\par\par\uc2 758 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2014\par 06:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, Aug 4 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic\par indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on\par Monday.\par     - - - - -\par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  Fears of further declines on Wall Street pressured Asian shares\par  on Monday, as concerns over geopolitical tensions and\par  Argentina's debt default eclipsed U.S. data that argued against\par  an earlier start to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's rate-tightening\par  cycle.                          \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par  Brent crude rose to $105 a barrel on Monday to come off of a\par  four-month low hit in the previous session, with worries about\par  global oversupply still outweighing concerns about violence in\par  the Middle East and North Africa.                    \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on            \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par  South African stocks gyrated but still ended lower on Friday\par  after the U.S. reported job growth slowed more than expected in\par  July and the unemployment rate rose, easing worries that\par  interest rates will rise soon.               \par      South Africa's rand snapped a four-day losing streak\par  against the dollar on Friday, helped mostly by U.S. jobs data\par  which supported the case for loose monetary policy in the\par  world's biggest economy.               \par  \par  AFRICA DEBT \par  Yields on Nigerian debt are expected to fall in the week ahead\par  while those in Kenya are seen steadying, traders\par  said.               \par  \par  U.S.- AFRICA SUMMIT\par  The United States will announce nearly $1 billion in business\par  deals, increase funding for peacekeeping and commit billions of\par  dollars to expanding food and power programs in Africa during a\par  summit this week, U.S. and development officials\par  say.               \par  \par  NIGERIA MARKETS\par  Nigeria's interbank lending rates were flat on Friday, trading\par  at an average of 11.12 percent, the same level they closed at\par  last week, but they are expected to climb next week as some\par  liquidity exits the banking system to fund cash reserve\par  requirements.               \par      Also, Nigeria plans to raise 195.17 billion naira ($1.21\par  billion) in short-dated treasury bills at an auction on\par  Wednesday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Friday.                \par  \par  NIGERIA PETROLEUM\par  Nigeria's President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goodluck Jonathan\f28 \uc2 \f2  has replaced the top four\par  executives at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Nigeria\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  National Petroleum Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2 , his\par  office said on Saturday, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in one of the country's\par  most powerful institutions and the source of 80 percent of\par  government revenues.                \par  \par  NIGERIA FLOUR MILLS\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Flour Mills of Nigeria\f28 \uc2 \f2               said on Friday its\par  full-year to March 31, pre-tax profit dropped 24.4 percent to\par  8.22 billion naira ($50.94 million), compared with 10.88\par  billion naira the previous year.                \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  Financial and telecoms stocks led Kenya's main share index\par  higher for a third consecutive day of gains on Friday. The\par  shilling        held steady against the dollar.                \par  \par  KENYA LAND\par  Kenya's President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Uhuru Kenyatta\f28 \uc2 \f2  has ordered the government to\par  repossess large areas of land in Lamu County, which has been\par  hit by recent attacks, saying land grabbing was helping fuel\par  instability on the north coast.               \par  \par  UGANDA ANTI-HOMOSEXUALITY LAW\par  Uganda's constitutional court on Friday overturned an\par  anti-homosexuality law that punished gay sex with long prison\par  sentences and was condemned by Western and other donors, some\par  of whom withheld aid in protest.               \par  \par  UGANDA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  The Ugandan shilling        gained on Friday against the dollar\par  after the country's constitutional court struck down an\par  anti-homosexuality law that punishes gay sex with long jail\par  sentences, traders said.                \par  \par  GHANA ECONOMY\par  Ghanaian President \f28 \uc2 \f2 John Mahama\f28 \uc2 \f2  has ordered his government to\par  open talks with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  on a programme\par  to help stabilise the economy and halt a slide in the cedi\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , officials said on Saturday.               \par  \par  IVORY COAST BOND\par  Ivory Coast will issue a 100 billion CFA franc ($205\par  million)five-year treasury bond with a 6 percent coupon on Aug.\par  4, the West African nation's treasury director Adama Kone said\par  on Saturday in a statement.               \par  \par  ZAMBIA COPPER\par  Diversified miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vedanta Resources Plc\f28 \uc2 \f2          said it was\par  open to a scrutiny of its Zambian copper business, which has\par  faced protests recently over allegedly not paying enough\par  taxes.               \par  \par  GUINEA IRON ORE MINING\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 ArcelorMittal\f28 \uc2 \f2           , the world's largest steelmaker, said\par  on Friday it had signed deals to purchase stakes in an iron ore\par  project in Guinea as it pushes to raise its mining output and\par  leverage its existing presence in the region.                \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-8-4T05:56:42.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140804ea84002xn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
