\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Markets: Trouble Ahead On The Frontier -- Barron's\b0\par\par\uc2 648 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2014\par 06:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par M7\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (FROM BARRON'S 4/14/14) \par    By Shuli Ren \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Frontier markets have been on a tear, benefiting in part from investor worries about major emerging-market countries like Brazil and China.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Since May, the \uc2 iShares MSCI Frontier 100 ETF\uc2  (ticker: FM) has returned 25%, while the \uc2 iShares MSCI Emerging Markets ETF\uc2  (EEM) has just broken even. This may be a brief star turn. Frontier \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are under pressure, and their two best performers -- the United Arab Emirates and Qatar -- will leave the MSCI frontier-markets index on June 2, without solid understudies.\par \par \uc2 This year, the effect of Federal Reserve "tapering is shifting from emerging markets to frontier markets," warns \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in a new research report. Argentina, which was downgraded from emerging to frontier market in 2009, started the trend in January, sending the peso down almost 20% against the dollar. In February, amid the Ukraine crisis and falling Russian ruble, Kazakhstan devalued the tenge by 19%, and Ukraine's hryvnia slumped 27%. Unlike emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which mostly float freely and adjust to changes continuously, frontier-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are heavily managed, or even pegged, which means they can require big adjustments once they can no longer maintain their value.\par \par \uc2 The UAE and Qatar -- about a third of the MSCI index -- have driven performance: In the past year, MSCI UAE returned 83%, and MSCI Qatar rose 32%. In the recent World Economic Outlook, \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  praised the UAE and Qatar for diversifying beyond oil, embarking on public investment programs, and for the 2020 World Expo and the 2022 World Cup.\par \par \uc2 Once the two Persian Gulf states leave in June, Citi Research estimates that Kuwait (29%) and Nigeria (17%) will make up about half of the index. Morocco, Argentina, Pakistan, and Kenya will each have about a 5% to 7% weight.\par \par \uc2 In contrast to the UAE and Qatar, Kuwait still sits on its black gold. The government only spent 8.3% of its total expenditures on development projects last year, down from 10.2% in 2010. Not surprisingly, in the past year, Kuwait underperformed the benchmark Frontier Market index by 8.4 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria is a wild card with lots of political risk. The country may have a hard time defending its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the naira, says \uc2 HSBC\uc2 . Nigeria has Russia-like problem in that it runs a sizable current-account surplus from oil exports, but needs continuous \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to offset persistent capital flight. In March, \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve fell by 8%, and the naira is off 2.2% this year.\par \par \uc2 Investors worry that next February's general election will be a repeat of 2007, marred by violence and allegations of rigging. Just a couple of months ago, President Goodluck Jonathan sacked \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Lamido Sanusi for "financial recklessness," after the respected economist accused state-owned Nigerian National Petroleum of socking away $50 billion in oil revenue that should have gone to government coffers. The figure was larger than the country's entire foreign reserve. Investors' apprehension about these issues has helped push the Global X Nigeria Index (NGE) down 9.7% in 2014.\par \par \uc2 If it overcomes these problems, there's lots to like. Nigeria is Africa's largest economy and has become less reliant on oil. Its services sector represents about half of gross domestic product, from less than 30% two decades ago. And the IMF expects GDP growth to accelerate to 7.1% this year from 6.3% in 2013.\par \par \uc2 Regardless, the new MSCI frontier markets index looks uninspiring and undiversified. Interestingly, as a nod to the problems, the MSCI recently started a consultation on potential methodological changes for the FM 100 Index.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 e-mail: shuli-ren@barrons.com\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 To subscribe to Barron's, visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.barrons.com/subscribe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.barrons.com/subscribe}}}\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 12, 2014 00:05 ET (04:05 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140412ea4c0001q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
