\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on March 3\b0\par\par\uc2 822 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 06:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, March 3 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic\par indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on\par Monday.\par     - - - - -\par  EVENTS:\par  *NIGERIA - \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's IFC and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nigeria's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holds\par  an event on sustainable banking in Africa's second-biggest\par  economy.  \par  *KENYA - \f28 \uc2 \f2 CFC Stanbic Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  releases its full year 2013\par  earnings results.\par  \par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  Stock prices plummeted while oil prices shot up on Monday as\par  escalating tensions between Russia and the West after Russia\par  bloodlessly seized a part of Ukraine.                 \par             \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par  Brent and U.S. crude oil rallied more than $2 per barrel to\par  multi-month highs on Monday, lifted by rising tension in\par  Ukraine after Russian President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vladimir Putin\f28 \uc2 \f2  declared he\par  had the right to invade his neighbour.                \par       \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par             \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  AFRICA DEBT \par  Nigerian Treasury bill yields are expected to rise next week\par  as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tightens liquidity to bolster the naira.\par  In Kenya, T-bill yields are set to fall in line with slowing\par  inflation.                  \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par  South Africa's rand softened against the dollar on Friday\par  after the revenue service reported a wider-than-expected\par  trade deficit for January, pointing to pressure on the\par  current account in the first quarter of the year.\par                 \par      Stocks ended higher on Friday, led by insurer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Old Mutual\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  which announced robust annual sales, and the main\par  Johannesburg index finished February with its biggest\par  monthly gain in seven months.                \par  \par  NIGERIA MARKETS\par  Nigerian interbank lending rates eased slightly on Friday to\par  an average of 10.75 percent, from 11 percent last week,\par  traders said, but they are seen rising next week on a coming\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  debit to meet cash reserves requirements\par  (CRR).                  \par      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Nigeria\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par  exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market minutes before it closed on Friday, selling\par  an undisclosed amount of dollars that enabled the naira to\par  reverse earlier losses, dealers said.               \par  \par  NIGERIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES\par  Nigeria's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves fell 6.75 percent\par  month-on-month to $40.25 billion as of Feb. 27, the bank's\par  latest data showed on Friday, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  boosted\par  its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to prop up the ailing naira\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .               \par  \par  NIGERIA SECURITY\par  Suspected Islamist militants have killed at least 85 people\par  in northeastern Nigeria, witnesses and officials said on\par  Sunday, in a further setback to President Goodluck\par  Jonathan's military campaign.                          \par  \par  ECOBANK AFRICA\par  The main shareholder in Ecobank         , one of the biggest\par  banks in sub-Saharan Africa, called on Saturday for its\par  Ivorian chief executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thierry Tanoh\f28 \uc2 \f2  to be dismissed\par  immediately.                \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  Kenya's main share index edged up on Friday, led higher by\par  sugar maker Mumias and banks, while the shilling was barely\par  moved after demand for dollars fizzled out.               \par  \par  KENYA KENGEN \par  Kenya's biggest power producer KenGen           aims to\par  raise 30 billion Kenyan shillings ($347 million) in 2014 to\par  fund its expansion plans, double the amount the firm\par  previously said it would seek, its chief executive said on\par  Friday.                \par  \par  KENYA NIC BANK\par  Kenya's NIC Bank          said on Friday it would issue\par  bonus shares after it reported an 11 percent rise in full\par  year pretax profit to 5.0 billion shillings ($57.90\par  million), helped by growth in its net interest income.\par                 \par  \par  KENYA CFC STANBIC HOLDINGS\par  Kenya's \f28 \uc2 \f2 CFC Stanbic Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2           posted a 57 percent\par  rise in 2013 pretax profit to 7.22 billion shillings ($84\par  million), in line with strong growth notched up by other\par  listed Kenyan financial institutions last year.\par                 \par  \par  UGANDA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 Uganda's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Friday it was selling foreign\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the third day this week it has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par  support the shilling        which has weakened by around 3\par  percent since donors withheld aid over an anti-gay law.\par                 \par  \par  TANZANIA GOLD\par  Tanzania's earnings from gold exports fell by 18.2 percent\par  in 2013, undermined by lower output and declining global\par  prices of the precious metal, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  report said on\par  Friday.                \par  \par  MAURITIUS MONETARY POLICY\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mauritius' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor called on Friday for more\par  independence in forming the monetary policy committee, weeks\par  after a rift with the finance minister over interest rate\par  levels on the Indian Ocean island.                \par  \par  GHANA MARKETS\par  The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Ghana\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Friday that the yield on its\par  91-day bill rose to 21.2304 percent at its Feb. 28 auction\par  from 21.0825 percent at the last auction.                \par  \par  MOZAMBIQUE POLITICS\par  Mozambique's ruling Frelimo party early on Sunday picked\par  Defence Minister Filipe Nyusi, a close ally of current\par  two-term President Armando Guebuza, to be its candidate for\par  an election in October that will choose the country's next\par  leader.                \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-3-6T05:10:21.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140303ea33005xx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
