\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Feb 27\b0\par\par\uc2 674 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2014\par 06:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, Feb 27 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic\par indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on\par Thursday.\par     - - - - -\par  EVENTS:\par  * ANGOLA - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to announce its decision on its\par  benchmark interest rate.\par  *KENYA - \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kenya Commercial Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2           and Equity Bank\par            release their full-year 2013 earnings results.\par  *KENYA - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  to auction 91-day Treasury\par  bills worth a total 3 billion shillings.\par  *ZAMBIA - Zambia to release consumer inflation data for\par  February.   \par  \par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  Asian shares struggled to find a solid footing on Thursday\par  as escalating tensions in Ukraine sent investors scurrying\par  to the safety of the dollar and U.S. Treasuries.\par                             \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par             \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par  South Africa's rand was weaker against the dollar on\par  Wednesday after Finance Minister Pravin Gordhan presented\par  the 2014 budget to parliament and as emerging market\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came under pressure.                \par      South African stocks recovered on Wednesday, as resource\par  stocks such as petrochemical group Sasol          and mining\par  company Assore          were lifted by the weaker rand and\par  short-term insurer Santam          gained on a surprise rise\par  in earnings.                \par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 NIGERIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKETS\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Nigeria\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with dollar sales to lift\par  the naira on Wednesday but strong demand for the U.S. dollar\par  outweighed the move.               \par  \par  NIGERIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES\par  Nigeria's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves fell to $40.68 billion as of Feb.\par  24, down 13.8 percent year-on-year, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  figures\par  showed on Wednesday.                         \par  \par  NIGERIA PETROLEUM\par  Nigeria will export around 1.73 million barrels per day\par  (bpd) of crude oil in April, down from 1.88 million bpd\par  planned in March, shipping lists seen by Reuters indicated\par  on Wednesday.                \par      \f28 \uc2 \f2 Royal Dutch Shell\f28 \uc2 \f2           said on Wednesday that it had\par  closed Nigeria's Nembe Creek Trunk oil pipeline on Saturday\par  to stop leakage caused by theft.                \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  Kenyan shares rose on Wednesday, led by oil and\par  manufacturing companies, and the shilling        overcame\par  early losses to finish unchanged against the dollar.\par                 \par  \par  KENYA KENGEN\par  Kenya's main electricity producer KenGen           reported\par  on Wednesday a 25 percent fall in pretax profit in the six\par  months to December, but forecast a stronger second half as\par  new power plants come online.                \par  \par  UGANDA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  The Ugandan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold dollars to support the\par  shilling        on Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened\par  more than 1.8 percent during the session on fears of more\par  aid cuts by Western donors over a law that toughened\par  punishments for gays.                        \par  \par  GHANA ECONOMY\par  Ghana's economy grew 5.5 percent in 2013, less than the 8\par  percent targeted by the government, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International\par  Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Wednesday.                \par      The country's annual producer price inflation rose\par  sharply to 23.3 percent year-on-year in January from 15.3\par  percent in December mainly on utility price hikes and the\par  decline of the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the government statistician\par  said.                \par  \par  GUINEA PROTEST\par  Protesters angered by the death of a young man in police\par  custody ransacked a police station and government buildings\par  in Guinea's main aluminium smelting town on Wednesday, local\par  residents said.               \par  \par  IVORY COAST COCOA\par  Armajaro Trading Ltd has offered to pay bonuses Ivory Coast\par  says cocoa farmers are owed by Ecom Agroindustrial Corp to\par  resolve a dispute which it fears could otherwise scupper its\par  takeover by the Swiss group, letters given to Reuters by\par  Armajaro showed.               \par  \par  ANGOLA LNG \par  A compressor leak at Angola's new liquefied natural gas\par  (LNG) export plant has delayed loading programmes and\par  reduced output at the $10 billion project, which is due to\par  shut for two months from July, a site manager\par  said.               \par  \par  ANGOLA BANKING\par  Russia's second-largest bank VTB           and state\par  conglomerate Rostec will buy a stake of around 20 percent in\par  Angolan bank Banco Privado Atlantico, VTB said on\par  Wednesday.               \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-3-2T05:05:07.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140227ea2r00594\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
