\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Feb 17\b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2014\par 08:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par moves and political events may affect African markets on Monday.\par     - - - ---\par  EVENTS:\par  RWANDA - The finance ministry issues more details on the\par  country's upcoming domestic bond for $18 million.\par  \par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  Asian shares built on their recent rally on Monday as\par  worries about emerging markets continued to ebb, sucking the\par  safe-haven support out of the U.S. dollar while giving\par  commodities a lift.            \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par  Brent futures slipped towards $109 a barrel on Monday as\par  disappointing U.S. economic data revived worries about\par  demand from the world's top oil consumer, but strong\par  consumption of heating fuels due to a cold spell checked\par  losses.      \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par             \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  AFRICA DEBT\par  Nigerian bond yields are likely to keep rising next week as\par  foreign investors sell their holdings amid concern about the\par  naira's depreciation. In Kenya, investor demand for a\par  15-year bond on sale next week is expected to be healthy.\par                  \par  \par  AFRICA GROWTH\par  Sub-Saharan Africa can meet growth expectations of more than\par  6 percent this year, despite a slowdown in China, but the\par  outlook for North Africa is more uncertain, the president of\par  the African Development Bank said on Friday.                \par  \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par  South Africa's rand was trading at three-week highs on\par  Friday as dollar weakness helped the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Africa's\par  biggest economy firm beyond the key 11 to the dollar level.\par                 \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA SHARES\par  South African stocks rallied on Friday after stumbling in\par  the previous session, with the Gold Mining Index         \par  leaping over 5 percent as bullion's spot price raced to\par  three-month highs above $1,300 an ounce.                \par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 NIGERIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKETS\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Nigeria\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday to help the\par  naira          recover to around 161.85 to the U.S. dollars,\par  after it weakened to around 164 earlier in the session.\par                 \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  East African Breweries dragged Kenyan shares lower after\par  reporting disappointing first half profits, while the\par  shilling        ended steady.                \par  \par  GHANA MARKETS\par  The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Ghana\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Friday that the yield on its\par  91-day bill rose to 20.7851 percent at its Feb. 14 auction\par  from 20.1248 percent at the last auction.                \par  \par  GHANA ECOBANK \par  Top executives at pan-African lender Ecobank         \par           have asked CEO \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thierry Tanoh\f28 \uc2 \f2  to step down to\par  resolve a crisis of leadership, according to an email sent\par  by the bank's deputy chief executive to its interim\par  chairman.                \par  \par  ANGOLA INFLATION\par  Angola's annual consumer inflation accelerated to 7.84\par  percent year-on-year in January from 7.69 percent in\par  December, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said on\par  Friday.                \par  \par      For the latest precious meta