\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  up after U.S. data; Latam stocks sink\b0\par\par\uc2 By Asher Levine and Natsuko Waki   \par \uc2 686 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2014\par 20:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO/LONDON, Feb 13 (Reuters) - Concerns over economic growth, corporate earnings and inflation drove Latin American stocks lower on Thursday, although most emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained against the dollar following disappointing U.S. retail data.\par \par \uc2 Yields on 10-year and 30-year U.S. bonds retreated from recent peaks, relieving pressure on South Africa's rand, the Turkish lira and the Hungarian forint, some of the worst-hit \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the sell-off that began last month. \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also rebounded after a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 U.S. retail sales fell unexpectedly in January, signaling slowing economic growth and raising the outlook among some investors for a slower reduction in the Federal Reserve's monetary stimulus program.\par \par \uc2 While some traders attributed the afternoon's broad strengthening of emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the weak figures, others saw a technical correction after recent losses, considering the impact of inclement weather on the U.S. data.\par \par \uc2 "A weak quarter, especially one for which the data is not particularly clean, will not alter the Fed's medium-term views of the underlying economy or the risk-reward of (monetary stimulus)," wrote \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  analysts in a note.\par \par \uc2 All of Latin America's major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened against the dollar, with Brazil's real up over 1 percent and Mexico's peso rising 0.2 percent. Chile's peso also gained as companies, mostly mining firms, sold dollars on the local market.\par \par \uc2 The region's stocks fared worse, with MSCI's Latin American stock index down 0.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 A plunge in \uc2 Banco do Brasil SA\uc2  shares helped drag Brazilian stocks down. The state-run lender posted worse-than-expected quarterly earnings and signalled a possible slowdown in lending this year.\par \par \uc2 Weaker-than-expected retail sales also sapped appetite for Brazilian equities, which have been battered over the past year on concerns over slow economic growth and higher interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "Some calculations now suggest gross domestic product could fall into negative territory in the fourth quarter, something that was (previously) out of the question," said Gustavo Mendon\u231\'00\'E7a, an economist with Saga Capital in Rio de Janeiro.\par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  analysts Marcelo Kfoury and Leonardo Porto on Thursday cut their outlook for Brazilian economic growth in 2014 to 1.3 percent from 1.8 percent previously.\par \par \uc2 Mexican shares also dropped, following weak earnings from conglomerate Alfa.\par \par \uc2 In Europe, concerns continued to grow over how Ukraine can prop up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pay off its debt. Russia suspended a $15 billion bailout after Ukrainian President Viktor Yanukovich sacked his prime minister late last month.\par \par \uc2 "Ukraine is on the knife-edge of solvency risk," said Gabriel Sterne, an economist at broker Exotix.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  brought in temporary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls last week after the hryvnia fell below 9 per dollar for the first time in five years. The bank said on Thursday controls may last longer than two weeks, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to fall.\par \par \uc2 Investors were not convinced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could continue to defend the hryvnia. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened further on Thursday, losing 1.5 percent against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's forint fell 0.4 percent against the euro , though strengthened against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Investors are watching inflation data due Friday for clues on whether rates will be cut again next week. Hungary's benchmark rate is already at a record-low 2.85 percent.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the Nigerian naira rebounded from a two-year low against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold an undisclosed amount of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lenders to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Nigerian stocks and bonds got hammered earlier in the session as investors sold off frontier-market assets.\par \par \uc2 Africa's second-largest economy and biggest oil producer has been a top frontier-market investment in recent years. But political instability is a concern before upcoming elections, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tightened reserve requirements.\par \par \uc2 \f2               \par               \par               \par               \par               \par               \par For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par               \par For TURKISH market report, see\par \par               \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For RUSSIAN market report, see\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-2-16T19:47:09.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140213ea2d00sju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
