\par\par \b \uc2 Nigerian naira falls; market  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  are no help\b0\par\par\uc2 164 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2014\par 15:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Feb 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's naira eased on Wednesday as demand for U.S. dollars overcame an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and an injection of dollars by a major oil firm.\par \par \uc2 The naira closed at 164.75 to the greenback, weaker than Tuesday's close of 164.10 naira.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \uc2 Nigerian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the local unit of \uc2 Royal Dutch Shell\uc2  sold an undisclosed amount of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lenders. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not help.\par \par \uc2 "Demand was strong ... while the dollar sales by both the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Shell was not enough to calm the market," one dealer said.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the naira dropped to its weakest in more than two years, but it recovered the following day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sustains its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the naira could weaken to 165 and above in the coming days," another dealer said.\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-2-15T14:27:24.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140212ea2c00pe2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
