\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria \highlight\uc2 's naira firms 1 pct after cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2013\par 17:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Aug 30 (Reuters) - The Nigerian naira gained 1 percent against the U.S. dollar on Friday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market to stem the local unit's decline.\par \par \uc2 The naira closed at 162.1 naira to the dollar, recovering from a 20-month low of 163.7 naira to the dollar on Thursday. Thursday's falls had happened because dollar liquidity was drained out by foreign investors repatriating proceeds from selling down some of their stock holdings, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars directly to some banks to ... provide support for the naira," one dealer said.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  calmed naira volatility and restored confidence in its willingness to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid speculation that it could lower the trading around the naira.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves declined marginally, by 0.23 percent month-on-month to $46.85 billion by Aug. 29, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures. Reserves have been stable because they bank has desisted from using them to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the same rate as in the past, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The bank hiked the cash reserve requirement for public sector deposits to 50 percent from 12 percent last month in a bid to tighten naira liquidity to help curb speculation, but it did little to quell dollar demand.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered the naira's target band against the dollar in November 2011, after months of monetary tightening steadied the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but failed to bring it back into the regulator's preferred trading range.\par \par \uc2 It moved the band target band to 150-160 naira to the U.S. dollar, compared with 145-155 naira previously.\par \par \uc2 But dealers said the bank was in a strong position to keep the naira in its current corridor.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the naira to gain more value as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increases the frequency of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and more dollar flows come in from oil companies," another dealer said. (Reporting by Oludare Mayowa; Editing by Chijioke Ohuocha and Tim Cocks)\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA NAIRA | AFN | ABN | D | M | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130830e98u000to\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
