\par\par \b \uc2 PRESS RELEASE: Fitch Assigns FBN Holdings Plc 'B' IDR\b0\par\par\uc2 985 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2013\par 15:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par The following is a press release from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2 : \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2 -London-17 May 2013: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  has assigned \f28 \uc2 \f2 FBN Holdings Plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  (FBNH) a Long-term Issuer Default Rating (IDR) of 'B' and Short-term IDR of 'B'. The Outlook on the Long-term IDR is Stable. A full list of rating actions is at the end of this announcement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The assignment of ratings to FBNH follows \uc2 First Bank of Nigeria Plc\uc2 's (now \uc2 First Bank of Nigeria Limited\uc2 , FBN) decision to adopt a holding company structure in line with new \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Nigeria\uc2  (CBN) guidelines. Under the new structure FBNH has become the 100% holding company of FBN which consolidates the group's banking \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . FBNH's non-banking subsidiaries include the capital markets businesses, insurance subsidiaries and microfinance bank. Together, the non-banking subsidiaries accounted for about 11% of consolidated assets at end-2012.\par \par \uc2 KEY RATING DRIVERS - IDRS, VR AND NATIONAL RATINGS\par \par \uc2 - FBNH's IDRs and VR are driven by and equalised with the VR of its 100%-banking subsidiary, FBN. This is supported by consolidated supervision by the CBN, common branding and management across the group and low levels of double leverage at the holding company stand-alone level. FBNH's National Ratings are mapped from its Long-term IDR.\par \par \uc2 RATING SENSITIVITIES - IDRS, VR AND NATIONAL RATINGS\par \par \uc2 - FBNH's IDRs, VR and National Ratings are sensitive to a change in FBN's VR which could improve in the longer-term once loan growth stabilises, accompanied by consistent asset quality indicators and maintenance of high levels of liquidity and appropriate Fitch Core Capital ratios. Downward pressure is limited in the short-term following significantly improved asset quality due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Asset Management Corporation of \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AMCON, a company tasked with cleaning up the non-performing loans in the sector) but could arise if loan impairment charges begin to have a significant impact on its long-term earnings and capitalisation following above sector-average credit growth in 2012.\par \par \uc2 KEY RATING DRIVERS AND SENSITIVITIES - SUPPORT RATING AND SUPPORT RATING FLOOR\par \par \uc2 - While support for FBNH from the authorities is possible, it has not been factored into Fitch's ratings. FBNH's Support Rating (SR) of '5' and Support Rating Floor (SRF) of 'NF' reflect the agency's view that while the authorities' propensity to support the banks in Nigeria remains high, the same level of support would not apply to holding companies.\par \par \uc2 The rating actions are as follows:\par \par \uc2 FBN Holdings Plc\par \par \uc2 - Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: assigned at 'B'. Stable Outlook\par \par \uc2 - Short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: assigned at 'B'\par \par \uc2 - National Long-term rating: assigned at 'A(nga)'\par \par \uc2 - National Short-term rating: assigned at 'F1(nga)'\par \par \uc2 - Viability Rating: assigned at 'b'\par \par \uc2 - Support Rating: assigned at '5'\par \par \uc2 - Support Rating Floor: assigned at 'NF'\par \par \uc2 First Bank of Nigeria Limited\par \par \uc2 - Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: unaffected at 'B+'. Stable Outlook\par \par \uc2 - Short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: unaffected at 'B'\par \par \uc2 - National Long-term rating: unaffected at 'A+(nga)'\par \par \uc2 - National Short-term rating: unaffected at 'F1(nga)'\par \par \uc2 - Viability Rating: unaffected at 'b'\par \par \uc2 - Support Rating: unaffected at '4'\par \par \uc2 - Support Rating Floor: unaffected at 'B+'\par \par \uc2 Contact:\par \par \uc2 Primary Analyst\par \par \uc2 - Mahin Dissanayake\par \par \uc2 - Director\par \par \uc2 - +44 20 3530 1618\par \par \uc2 - Fitch Ratings Limited\par \par \uc2 - 30 North Colonnade\par \par \uc2 - London E14 5GN\par \par \uc2 Secondary Analyst\par \par \uc2 - Bjorn Norrman\par \par \uc2 - Director\par \par \uc2 - +44 20 3530 1330\par \par \uc2 Committee Chairperson\par \par \uc2 - Philip Smith\par \par \uc2 - Senior Director\par \par \uc2 - +44 20 3530 1091\par \par \uc2 Media Relations: Hannah Huntly, London, Tel: +44 20 3530 1153, Email: hannah.huntly@fitchratings.com.\par \par \uc2 Additional information is available on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.fitchratings.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Applicable criteria, 'Global Financial Institutions Rating Criteria', dated 15 August 2012, 'Rating FI Subsidiaries and Holding Companies', dated 10 August 2012, 'Evaluating Corporate Governance', dated 12 December 2012 and 'National Ratings', dated 19 January 2011 are available on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.fitchratings.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Note to Editors: Fitch's National ratings provide a relative measure of creditworthiness for rated entities in countries with relatively low international sovereign ratings and where there is demand for such ratings. The best risk within a country is rated 'AAA' and other credits are rated only relative to this risk. National ratings are designed for use mainly by local investors in local markets and are signified by the addition of an identifier for the country concerned, such as 'AAA(nga)' for National ratings in Nigeria. Specific letter grades are not therefore internationally comparable.\par \par \uc2 Applicable Criteria and Related Research\par \par \uc2 - Global Financial Institutions Rating Criteria\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com/creditdesk/reports/report_frame.cfm?rpt_id=686181"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.fitchratings.com/creditdesk/reports/report_frame.cfm?rpt_id=686181}}}\par \par \uc2 - Rating FI Subsidiaries and Holding Companies\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com/creditdesk/reports/report_frame.cfm?rpt_id=679209"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.fitchratings.com/creditdesk/reports/report_frame.cfm?rpt_id=679209}}}\par \par \uc2 - Evaluating Corporate Governance\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com/creditdesk/reports/report_frame.cfm?rpt_id=694649"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.fitchratings.com/creditdesk/reports/report_frame.cfm?rpt_id=694649}}}\par \par \uc2 - National Ratings Criteria\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com/creditdesk/reports/report_frame.cfm?rpt_id=595885"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.fitchratings.com/creditdesk/reports/report_frame.cfm?rpt_id=595885}}}\par \par \uc2 Additional Disclosure\par \par \uc2 - Solicitation Status\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com/gws/en/disclosure/solicitation?pr_id=791403"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.fitchratings.com/gws/en/disclosure/solicitation?pr_id=791403}}}\par \par \uc2 - ALL FITCH CREDIT RATINGS ARE SUBJECT TO CERTAIN LIMITATIONS AND DISCLAIMERS. PLEASE READ THESE LIMITATIONS AND DISCLAIMERS BY FOLLOWING THIS LINK: HTTP://FITCHRATINGS.COM/UNDERSTANDINGCREDITRATINGS. IN ADDITION, RATING DEFINITIONS AND THE TERMS OF USE OF SUCH RATINGS ARE AVAILABLE ON THE AGENCY'S PUBLIC WEBSITE 'WWW.FITCHRATINGS.COM'. PUBLISHED RATINGS, CRITERIA AND METHODOLOGIES ARE AVAILABLE FROM TH