\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on March 22\b0\par\par\uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 06:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, March 22 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on Friday.\par \par \uc2 - - - - -\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS\par \par \uc2 Asian shares hovered near their lowest in nearly three months on\par \par \uc2 Friday and the euro was under pressure as investors grew concerned\par \par \uc2 about a possible debt default by Cyprus and deteriorating economic\par \par \uc2 activity in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 WORLD OIL PRICES\par \par \uc2 Brent crude held above $107 a barrel on Friday, but was still on\par \par \uc2 track for a second straight week of losses as Cyprus scrambled to\par \par \uc2 raise money to avert a financial meltdown that could disrupt the euro\par \par \uc2 zone's recovery and diminish its oil demand.\par \par \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS\par \par \uc2 For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par \par \uc2 AFRICA STOCKS\par \par \uc2 For the latest news on African stocks, click on\par \par \uc2 AFRICA \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Kenya's shilling is seen under pressure from market concerns about a\par \par \uc2 legal challenge to this month's presidential election and routine\par \par \uc2 end-month dollar demand, while \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are seen\par \par \uc2 keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's naira rangebound.\par \par \uc2 SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par \par \uc2 South African financial markets reopen on Friday after remaining\par \par \uc2 closed for a national holiday on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA POWER\par \par \uc2 All of the preferred bidders for the 15 electricity firms that\par \par \uc2 Nigeria is privatising met a deadline on Thursday to pay a quarter of\par \par \uc2 their bids, the government said, a milestone in the country's efforts\par \par \uc2 to end crippling power shortages.\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA OIL SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 Nigeria will make a second $1 billion withdrawal from its Excess\par \par \uc2 Crude Account (ECA) by next month to distribute to its three tiers of\par \par \uc2 government for projects, reducing its oil savings to $6.82 billion,\par \par \uc2 the state minister for finance said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA ECOBANK SUSPENSION\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's stock market regulator said on Thursday it had suspended\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Ecobank          from all capital market activities because of\par irregularities surrounding a loan.                \par KENYA MARKETS\par The Kenyan shilling        edged down on Thursday as importers bought\par dollars ahead of the usual month-end rush, while shares dipped for\par the seventh straight session.                \par KENYA T-BILLS\par The weighted average yield on Kenya's benchmark 91-day Treasury bills\par          rose to 10.318 percent at an oversubscribed sale on\par Thursday from 10.097 percent at last week's sale, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par said.                \par GHANA STOCKS\par The GSE Composite index extends its winning streak to nine\par consecutive days as shares in banking, energy and consumer goods\par stocks rally.                \par IVORY COAST \par UK-based emerging markets power company Globeleq has begun\par construction of a 139-megawatt expansion at its thermal power station\par in Ivory Coast, the company said on Thursday.                \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TANZANIA OIL RESERVES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tanzania Petroleum Development Corporation is seeking oil products\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for delivery over a one-year period to build a National Strategic\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Petroleum Reserve, a tender document showed on Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UGANDA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Ugandan shilling fell 0.4 percent against the dollar on\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wednesday, weakened by growing demand for the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 commercial banks and the manufacturing and energy sectors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MAURITIUS TRADE\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Mauritius trade deficit narrowed 3.6 percent to 6.21 billion\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mauritius rupees ($199.36 million) in January from a year ago on\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher exports, official data showed on Thursday.                \par SOUTH SUDAN OIL    \par South Sudan said on Thursday it is pressing ahead with studies into\par new oil pipelines to Kenya and Djibouti following a deal to restore\par exports through onetime civil war foe Sudan.                \par   For the latest precious metals report click on        \par   For the latest base metals report click on         \par   For the latest crude oil report click on       \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 AFRICA-FACTORS/ | AFN | RBN | ABN | E | D | M | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130322e93m00071\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
