\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria \highlight\uc2  naira gains vs dlr after cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 14:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Add background, details)\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, March 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's naira strengthened 0.56 percent against the U.S dollar on the interbank market on Friday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollar directly to lenders to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \uc2 The naira closed 158.70 to the dollar, compared with 159.60 the previous day.\par \par \uc2 The local unit had fallen to its weakest in more than seven months on Wednesday and fell further on Thursday due to demand pressure from importers and waning dollar supply from offshore investors buying local debt.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market today to save the naira from depreciating further," one dealer said.\par \par \uc2 The naira has been trading around 157 levels in recent months, supported by dollar flows from offshore investors buying government bonds, after \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  included Nigeria's sovereign debt in its emerging market bond index in October.\par \par \uc2 But falling yields on local debt since then has made Nigerian bonds less attractive for foreign investors, thereby curbing the influx of dollars.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market today signals a positive outlook for the naira. It shows that the regulator is willing to stop the rapid depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and ready to defend it," another dealer said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Oludare Mayowa; Editing by Tim Cocks)\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA-NAIRA/ (UPDATE 1) | AFN | ABN | D | M | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130315e93f000u5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
