\par\par \b \uc2 RPT- \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria \highlight\uc2  naira surges vs dollar on Cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2012\par 17:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to add topic codes)\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, June 18 (Reuters) - The Nigerian naira rose to its highest level in three weeks against the U.S. dollar on the interbank market on Monday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and speculation mounted of a planned dollar sale by the state oil firm.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 161.45 to the dollar on the interbank market, the level last seen on June 4, and firmer than the 163.25 a dollar it closed at on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the volatility continued intraday when the naira fell to as low as 163.90 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold large dollars to some lenders, which provided support for the naira and calmed the market.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did the magic to save the naira today otherwise, it would have crossed the 164 naira to the dollar mark," one dealer said.\par \par \uc2 "We also had the speculations that the NNPC will be selling dollar on Tuesday, which helped provide support."\par \par \uc2 Traders said additional $13.7 million was sold by two oil companies, Addax and a unit of \uc2 ExxonMobil\uc2 , which also helped to lift the market.\par \par \uc2 The Nigerian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has consistently weakened against the dollar in the last two months on the back of strong dollar demand, declining supply from multinational oil companies and mass exit of the local debt market by offshore investors fleeing to safe havens because of the Eurozone debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 "If the NNPC finally sells dollar in the market this week, we see the naira strengthening to around 160 to the dollar level," another dealer said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Oludare Mayowa; Editing by Tim Cocks)\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA-NAIRA/  (REPEAT) | AFN | ABN | D | M | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120618e86i000xs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
