\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Nigeria cbank takes new steps to stabilise naira\b0\par\par\uc2 516 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2011\par 14:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Cbank says to sell dollars directly into market\par \par \uc2 * Banks' net open positions upped to 3 pct vs 1 pct\par \par \uc2 * Naira trade volatile, weakens on Friday\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background, quote)\par \par \uc2 By Oludare Mayowa\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Oct 21 (Reuters) - Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it will sell U.S. dollars both directly into the market and at auctions, while it lifted the amount of dollars banks' can hold in reserve, in a continued effort to stabilise the naira \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 The regulator said it would raise the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  net open position limit banks can hold to 3 pct from 1 pct of shareholders' funds from Monday, less than two weeks after slashing limits to help protect the naira.\par \par \uc2 Net open position is the amount of dollars banks can hold relative to shareholders' funds. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered it to 1 percent from 5 percent on Oct. 10 to free up dollar supply to the interbank market but traders complained the market was almost brought to a halt by the decision.\par \par \uc2 The move had curbed lenders ability to hold dollar reserves to meet customer needs, leading to volatile trading at the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Some analysts said position limits at 1 percent could have negatively weighed on banks' revenues.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it will sell dollars directly into the interbank market and continue providing greenback at its official twice weekly auctions. It provides dollar liquidity to meet high demand and help support the naira.\par \par \uc2 "In the continuing effort to sustain stability in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2  shall from time to time \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the interbank market. This is in addition to (auctions)," it said in a letter to banks.\par \par \uc2 The naira hit an all-time low against the dollar prior to an emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting last week as worsening global economic conditions curbed risk appetite and dollar demand from importers and speculators increased.\par \par \uc2 The naira has been volatile in thin trade this week. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 159.30 to the dollar in the interbank market on Friday, weaker than 154.60 on Thursday but firmer than the record low of 167.80.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates by 2.75 pct to 12 pct and implemented several other tightening measures to help protect the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at its emergency meeting on Oct. 10.\par \par \uc2 It has also been selling dollars at auction and directly into the market. It offered to sell $200 million to some lenders in a special \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday but later retracted the sale.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the regulator sold $103.28 million at a cut-off rate of 150 naira to the dollar at an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, helping to provide some liquidity in the market, which helped the naira to recover.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  could help narrow the wide margin between official and interbank trading rates and reduce the volatility in the market.\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Joe Brock; editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA-CBANK/  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111024e7al000xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
