\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Head: Not  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  Right Now On  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2011\par 17:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 22 Sep 2011 11:39 EDT *DJ  Nigeria \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Head: Still Expect Net Inflows Into Country\par \par \uc2 22 Sep 2011 12:25 EDT DJ  Nigeria \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Still Expects Inflows\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Anjali Cordeiro \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Despite growing turmoil in global financial markets, the head of Nigeria's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said his country still expects to see net inflows of money coming into the country and that it isn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the moment to shore up its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have come under pressure, raising worries about big outflows from these countries and increasing the chances that central banks will have to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stop their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from falling too much.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the last few months, Nigeria has seen an increase in inflows, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor, Sanusi Lamido Sanusi, said. "If that continues we are able to maintain exchange rates within our band without losing reserves," he said. Still, inflation remains a pressure in many emerging nations, including Nigeria.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The governor acknowledged the local inflationary and exchange rate pressures the country faces. "We think it will be difficult to keep [inflation] in the single digits for a long time without further tightening," he said to reporters after a panel in Washington, adding that without tighter fiscal policy, monetary policy will have to be tighter.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Anjali Cordeiro; Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2200; anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 22, 2011 12:25 ET (16:25 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110922e79m004oy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
