\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Jan 21\b0\par\par\uc2 802 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2011\par 06:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Jan 21 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on Friday.\par \par \uc2 - - - - -\par \par \uc2 EVENTS\par \par \uc2 * Nigeria expected to launch its debut $500 million Eurobond after investor roadshows in United States and Europe.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Uganda\uc2  holds a news conference. The bank said on Wednesday it would adopt a more aggressive stance towards the shillings exchange rate versus the dollar after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its fifth record low of 2011.\par \par \uc2 * Mauritius' \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions Treasury bills of various maturities.\par \par \uc2 * Ugandan President Yoweri Museveni on second of a three-day state visit to South Africa.\par \par \uc2 - - - - - -\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS\par \par \uc2 Asian stocks slipped and commodities paused on Friday after a recent selloff on worries that rising inflation may invite aggressive policy tightening and hurt growth in the world's engines like China and India. [ID:nTOE70K01I]\par \par \uc2 AFRICAN MARKETS\par \par \uc2 For all the latest news on African stocks click on [.J]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par \par \uc2 South Africa's rand went to a seven-week low against the greenback on Thursday, testing key technical levels on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying, but recouped some of the losses after the Bank left interest rates unchanged. [ID:nLDE70J21H]\par \par \uc2 IVORY COAST CRISIS\par \par \uc2 Tougher action, possibly including force, is the only way to make Ivory Coast incumbent Laurent Gbagbo step down after mediation failed, rival presidential claimant Alassane Ouattara said on Thursday. [ID:nLDE70J1YU]\par \par \uc2 For more Ivory Coast stories, click on [ID:nCOC754498]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH SUDAN REFERENDUM\par \par \uc2 For stories on south Sudan's referendum, click on [ID:nLDE70708L]\par \par \uc2 AFRICA \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Ghana's cedi <GHS=> looks set to hit a lifetime low against the dollar next week, while Uganda's shilling <UGX=> should continue its rebound from an unprecedented slump that prompted stiff \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nLDE70J1B0]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 NIGERIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  MARKETS\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's all-share index <.NGSEINDEX> rose for the second consecutive day, up 1 percent to 27,575 points with banks among the top gainers. The rise brought cumulative gains by the index since the start of the year to 10 percent.\par \par \uc2 Also, Nigeria sold 60 billion naira ($393 million) in 5-year and 3-year sovereign bonds <0#NGTSY=> at its first debt auction of the year, the Debt Management Office (DMO) said on Thursday. [ID:nLDE70J0Y7]\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA EUROBOND\par \par \uc2 Nigeria has issued guidance for its $500 million debut Eurobond indicating a yield of around 7 percent, higher than that of West African peer Ghana, market sources said on Thursday. [ID:nLDE70J1TI]\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA SPENDING\par \par \uc2 Nigerian President Goodluck Jonathan's top advisers on Thursday urged him to cut the rising cost of government by merging ministries and agencies, freeing up funds for development projects. [ID:nLDE70J26R]\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA RESERVES\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects a drop in foreign reserves to end due to higher oil prices, tighter monetary policy, and stronger capital markets and sees no need to let the naira weaken, Governor Lamido Sanusi said. [ID:nLDE70J0WU]\par \par \uc2 KENYA MARKETS\par \par \uc2 The Nairobi Stock Exchange's benchmark NSE-20 share index <.NSE20> fell to its lowest level for 11 sessions, closing down 0.22 percent at 4,537.30 points. The broader all share index <.NASI> shed 0.14 percent to settle at 100.69 points.\par \par \uc2 The shilling <KES=> ended trade at 81.05/15, a touch weaker than Wednesday's close of 81.00/10.\par \par \uc2 Also, the yield on Kenya's 91-day Treasury bills inched up to 2.455 percent at auction, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday, up from 2.409 percent at the previous sale. [ID:nLDE70J1N9]\par \par \uc2 KENYA SAFARICOM BOND\par \par \uc2 Safaricom\uc2 's second tranche of its five-year medium-term note worth 4.5 billion shillings ($55.5 million) was fully subscribed, the Kenyan mobile phone operator's chief executive said on Thursday. [ID:nLDE70J0LF]\par \par \uc2 KENYA WIND POWER\par \par \uc2 Plans for a delayed 300 MW wind farm in Kenya can now proceed after lenders agreed to rely on the government's assurance that it backed the plan, instead of proper guarantees, the chairman of the project said. [ID:nLDE70J0AP]\par \par \uc2 MAURITIUS PRIVATE EQUITY\par \par \uc2 Mauritius private equity group Ciel Capital plans to venture into Kenya, east Africa's biggest economy, in the first half and is in talks with key players in various sectors, a senior partner said. [ID:nLDE70J0I0]\par \par \uc2 ZAMBIA CHINA INVESTMENT\par \par \uc2 Chinese investment in Zambia is expected to more than double to $2.4 billion in 2011, driven mainly by investments in mining and manufacturing, the southern African nation's trade minister said on Thursday. [ID:nLDE70J0U6]\par \par \uc2 COMMODITIES\par \par \uc2 For the latest precious metals report click on [GOL/]\par \par \uc2 For the latest base metals report click on [MET/L]\par \par \uc2 For the lates