\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Jan 10\b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2011\par 06:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Jan 10 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on Monday.\par \par \uc2 - - - - -\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS\par \par \uc2 Mounting fears over sovereign debt in the euro zone kept the euro tethered to four-month lows against the dollar on Monday, with investors nervous ahead of a flurry of bond sales from the region's weaker states. [ID:nTOE709019]\par \par \uc2 WORLD FOOD PRICES\par \par \uc2 The world's biggest economies are working to find ways to bring down soaring food prices, a G20 official said on Friday, as top exporter Thailand vowed to keep rice supply steady and avert a repeat of the 2008 food crisis. [ID:nL3E7C70I1]\par \par \uc2 For more on world food prices, click on [ID:nLDE7051AF]\par \par \uc2 AFRICAN MARKETS\par \par \uc2 For all the latest news on African stocks click on [.J]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par \par \uc2 South African resource-heavy stocks slipped on Friday as a stronger dollar induced investors to take profit from firmer lining shares. The rand reversed earlier losses against the greenback despite data showing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took advantage of its gains in December to build up foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. [ID:nLDE7061HO]\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA POLITICS\par \par \uc2 Nigeria enters the most important three months of its recent political history this week, beginning elections which could chart its path for further reform or plunge its most volatile regions back into violence. [ID:nLDE70803R]\par \par \uc2 For more Nigeria politics stories, click on [ID:nLDE70101O]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH SUDAN REFERENDUM\par \par \uc2 Millions of jubilant south Sudanese voted on Sunday in an independence referendum which could cut Africa's biggest country in two and deprive the north of most of its lucrative oil. [ID:nMCD944984]\par \par \uc2 For more Sudan referendum stories, click on [ID:nLDE70708L]\par \par \uc2 IVORY COAST CRISIS\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's former President Olusegun Obasanjo ended a day of mediation in Ivory Coast's crisis on Sunday, saying he was optimistic it could be resolved but not ruling out military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to oust leader Laurent Gbagbo. [ID:nLDE7080HZ]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 NIGERIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  MARKETS\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's all-share index <.NGSEINDEX> ended a three-day rally on Friday, falling 1.26 percent to 26,168 points, dragged down by losses in banking, cement and telecoms stocks. [ID:nLDE7061II]\par \par \uc2 Nigeria plans to go ahead with its delayed $500 million debut Eurobond in two to three weeks and expects a bill to create a sovereign wealth fund to pass under the current administration, the finance minister said on Friday. [ID:nLDE7060JC]\par \par \uc2 KENYA MARKETS\par \par \uc2 The Kenyan shilling <KES=> weakened slightly against the dollar on Friday, while the stock exchange's main share index rose to a near two-month high on the back of gains that were led by banks. [ID:nLDE70611T]\par \par \uc2 Kenya's official usable \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were unchanged last week at $3.466 billion. [ID:nLDE706159]\par \par \uc2 MAURITIUS BILLS\par \par \uc2 The weighted average yield on 91-day Treasury bills fell to 2.0 percent at auction on Friday. [ID:nLDE7060ZN]\par \par \uc2 ZAMBIA BILLS\par \par \uc2 The weighted average yield on 91-day Treasury bills fell to 7.27 percent at auction. [ID:nLDE7060BX]\par \par \uc2 COMMODITIES\par \par \uc2 For the latest precious metals report click on [GOL/]\par \par \uc2 For the latest base metals report click on [MET/L]\par \par \uc2 For the latest crude oil report click on [O/L]\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AFRICA-FACTORS/|LANGEN|SF|AFN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110110e71a0008d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
