\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Sept 20\b0\par\par\uc2 688 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2010\par 07:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Sept 20 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on Monday.\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 EVENTS\par \par \uc2 * NAIROBI - Kenya's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Njuguna Ndung'u hosts a conference on how to extend insurance services to more people in east Africa's largest economy.\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS\par \par \uc2 The dollar was on the defensive and gold held near a record high on Monday as possible further Federal Reserve moves to increase money supply weighed on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and boosted alternative assets. [ID:nSGE68J03X]\par \par \uc2 AFRICAN MARKETS\par \par \uc2 For all the latest news on African stocks click on [.J]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par \par \uc2 South Africa's rand steadied against the dollar on Friday, with dealers reluctant to take positions ahead of the weekend and a ruling ANC policy meeting that will discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  next week. [ID:nLDE68G1KT]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 NIGERIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  MARKETS\par \par \uc2 Guaranty Trust Bank\uc2  (GTBank) <GUARANT.LG> rose almost five percent after the Nigerian lender said it would divest all non-banking divisions in compliance with a new regulatory directive.\par \par \uc2 GTBank outperformed Nigeria's all-share index <.NGSEINDEX>, which ended broadly flat at 22,993.77 points.\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's consumer inflation rose to 13.7 percent year-on-year in August from 13.0 percent the previous month, the National Bureau of Statistics said on Friday. [ID:nLDE68G1VS]\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA POLITICS\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's national security adviser has resigned to run against President Goodluck Jonathan in the ruling party primaries next month, raising the stakes ahead of presidential elections due in January. [ID:nLDE68I03B]\par \par \uc2 KENYA MARKETS\par \par \uc2 The Kenyan shilling <KES=> weakened against the dollar on Friday although traders saw the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fundamentals remaining strong, while stocks gained in generally light trading. [ID:nLDE68G16C]\par \par \uc2 The east African nation's benchmark 20-share Index <.NSE20> closed up 0.19 percent at 4549.87 points, with a strong performance from the power sector. [ID:nLDE68G16C]\par \par \uc2 KENYA POWER\par \par \uc2 Trade unions have called off a strike set for Monday by workers at Kenya's sole power supplier after reaching a deal over most of their grievances, a power sector union leader said on Sunday. [ID:nLDE68I01T]\par \par \uc2 AFRICA BHARTI\par \par \uc2 Bharti Airtel\uc2  has selected IBM to manage the computing technology and services running its newly acquired mobile networks in 16 African countries, the companies said on Friday. [ID:nSGE68G09I]\par \par \uc2 GHANA DEBT\par \par \uc2 The average weighted yield on Ghana's 91-day Treasury bill edged down to 12.54 percent from 12.60 percent on Friday. [ID:nLDE68G1W7]\par \par \uc2 ZAMBIA SPENDING\par \par \uc2 Zambia, Africa's top producer of copper, expects state spending to total 71.7 trillion kwacha ($15.54 bln) over the next three years, the nation's treasury said in a statement on Sunday. [ID:LDE68I09O]\par \par \uc2 MAURITIUS ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 Mauritius' current account deficit narrowed in the second quarter from a year earlier as a higher capital account surplus partly offset a wider trade deficit, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday. [ID:nLDE68G17V]\par \par \uc2 MAURITIUS SUGAR\par \par \uc2 Mauritian sugar manufacturer and agricultural producer Savannah made a pretax loss of 44.1 million rupees ($1.4 million) in its last financial year, it reported on Friday, because of low sugar prices. [ID:nLDE68G1E2]\par \par \uc2 RWANDA ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 Consumer prices in Rwanda rose 1.04 percent in August from July, slowing the rate of deflation to 1.39 percent from 2.22 percent a month earlier, official data showed on Friday. [ID:nLDE68G0JO]\par \par \uc2 MAURITANIA SECURITY\par \par \uc2 Mauritanian military forces killed 12 members of al Qaeda's North African wing and suffered six fatalities in fighting along the border with Mali, the Defence Ministry said on Saturday. The clash is the latest sign of an escalation in the battle between Saharan countries and al Qaeda in the Islamic Maghreb (AQIM). [ID:nLDE68H03P]\par \par \uc2 For the top emerging markets news, double click on [nTOPEMRG]\par \par \uc2 COMMODITIES\par \par \uc2 For the latest precious metals report click on [GOL/]\par \par \uc2 For the latest base metals report click on [MET/L]\par \par \uc2 For the latest crude oil report click on [O/L]\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AFRICA-FACTORS/|LANGEN|SF|AFN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100920e69k0008u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
