\par\par \b \uc2 More turbulence in store for African  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 840 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2010\par 14:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 *** Reuters has launched a new weekly report looking at short-term prospects for six African \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , expanding its East African \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report to incorporate a weekly outlook for Nigeria, Zambia and Ghana.\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, May 20 (Reuters) - International investor aversion to emerging market assets is likely to weigh on African \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  next week, though some may start to rebound after several days of heavy selling.\par \par \uc2 KENYA\par \par \uc2 The shilling <KES=> fell heavily this week, breaking the 79.00 mark against the dollar for the first time in more than a year on the back of continued concerns about the performance of the euro. It may hit 80.00 before starting to recoup losses.\par \par \uc2 "The euro woes are still bearing heavily on the performance of the shilling," said Chris Muiga, senior trader at Kenya Commercial Bank.\par \par \uc2 "It seems like we are headed towards 80. I think the next level is a taste of 80 before we see a reversal," said Solomon Alubala, trader at Co-operative Bank.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, commercial banks were quoting the shilling at 79.10/20 compared to a Wednesday close of 79.15. It last traded at these levels in late April 2009.\par \par \uc2 UGANDA\par \par \uc2 Uganda's shilling <UGX=> hit a seven-month low this week due to concerns emanating from the euro zone, and demand for dollars from the energy sector.\par \par \uc2 The unit is expected to trade in a 2,180-2,200 range against the dollar over coming days, after closing at 2,215 on Wednesday. The previous Wednesday's close was 2,150.\par \par \uc2 "We may continue to see a weaker shilling though we expect some correction in the rates in the coming week as corporate demand eases next week," said Faisal Bukenya, head of market making at Barclays Bank Uganda.\par \par \uc2 Other traders said scant dollar flows into the market would continue to undermine the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The shilling is likely to shed more value in the days ahead. We anticipate a pick-up in corporate demand towards the end of the month," said another trader at a commercial bank.\par \par \uc2 Traders are also watching for \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 NIGERIA\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The naira <NGN=D1> may buck the trend and firm against the dollar as traders anticipate huge dollar inflows from energy companies, including state oil firm NNPC.\par \par \uc2 It was trading at 151.77 to the dollar on Thursday, compared to 151.05 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "We are anticipating month-end dollar sales by some energy companies, including NNPC, by next week which could ease pressure on demand," one dealer said.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said dollar demand remained strong.\par \par \uc2 GHANA\par \par \uc2 The cedi is seen trading in a narrow band of $1.41-$1.42 next week as the market focuses on prospects of oil revenues in late-2010 or early next year.\par \par \uc2 "That tends to offset the fundamentals," Samir Gadio of Rencap Securities said of expectations of revenues from the Jubilee oilfield, noting that otherwise Ghana would continue to run a relatively high current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 That deficit stood at around 8 percent of output by the end of 2009 but analysts say strong gold and cocoa prices and the impact of lower imports could help bring it down in 2010.\par \par \uc2 Sampson Akligoh of Accra-based Databank also saw the cedi underpinned in the medium-term and forecast a 1.5 percent appreciation against the dollar over the course of 2010.\par \par \uc2 Akligoh said that despite recent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves to cut the prime rate to 15 percent, the yield on the three-year bond available to foreign investors remained sufficiently attractive to keep portfolio inflows buoyant.\par \par \uc2 ZAMBIA\par \par \uc2 The kwacha <ZMK=> is likely to strengthen after two weeks of foreigners dumping local treasury bills and buying dollars.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the kwacha to appreciate to around 4,900 in the coming week mainly because of profit taking ... after (the dollar) breached the psychological mark of 5,000," Finance Bank treasurer Miles Sampa said.\par \par \uc2 The unit, which tends to track world copper prices because of Zambia's heavy reliance on copper exports, hit 5,130 on May 7 after lurching outside a 4,600-4,700 trading range that has prevailed for most of the previous eight months.\par \par \uc2 TANZANIA\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks quoted the shilling <TZS=> at 1,440/1,448 on Thursday, compared with 1,420 at Wednesday's close after a turbulent trading session in which the unit fell as low as 1,470. Last Wednesday's close was 1,406/1,415.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the shilling could weaken further due to tight dollar supply, predicting a 1,470-1,500 range in the coming days.\par \par \uc2 "The shilling might depreciate even further next month with the absence of inflows from agriculture. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in the market," said Esther Manase, a trader at Standard Chartered Bank Tanzania.\par \par \uc2 Between last Wednesday and Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Tanzania\uc2  traded $17 million on its Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market, according to statistics on its website.\par \par \uc2 AFRICA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|AFN|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100520e65k001n5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
