\par\par \b \uc2 Nigerian interbank rates climb on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  purchases\b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2008\par 17:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Dec 12 (Reuters) - Nigerian interbank interest rates rose to 9.83 percent on average this week from 8.0 percent last week, driven partly by a large outflow to the purchase of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The secured Open Buy Back (OBB) climbed from 7 percent to 9.00 percent, below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark rate of 9.75 percent, overnight rose to 10 percent from 8.00 percent, while call closed at 10.5 percent compared 9.00 percent previously.\par \par \uc2 "Interest rates went up as a result of the outflows to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold over $2 billion within two days," one dealer said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has consistently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since last week Wednesday by selling dollars to retail banks to help stabilise the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has depreciated by about 10 percent in the last three weeks.\par \par \uc2 Bankers said the rates would have risen higher but for the inflow in repaid matured treasury bills which provided liquidity as many banks did not reinvest the funds in the bills.\par \par \uc2 "We believe that rates will remain stable next week because of the anticipated inflow of December budgetary allocations into the system," another banker said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Oludare Mayowa)\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA-INTERBANK/|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|AFN|RBN|RNP|D