\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Nigerian naira dips to 130 vs dlr as cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Oludare Mayowa   \par \uc2 534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2008\par 17:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background)\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Dec 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $900 million to retail banks on Friday at its second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this week, allowing the naira to depreciate further against the U.S dollar.\par \par \uc2 Economists say it is in Nigeria's interests for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall as the world's eighth-biggest oil exporter tries to mitigate the effects of lower global demand for crude, which is eating into its foreign earnings.\par \par \uc2 A weaker naira gives the government greater spending power in naira terms for every dollar earned, helping sub-Saharan Africa's second-biggest economy to manage a widening deficit.\par \par \uc2 But the speed of the depreciation in recent days -- around 10 percent since the middle of last week -- has unnerved Nigeria's interbank market, which has long been used to the naira trading in a tight band against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold about $900.13 million to retail banks at a cut-off rate of 130 to the dollar," one dealer said.\par \par \uc2 Another dealer said the spread had been 130-131.50 naira, compared with a level of around 117 in the middle of last week.\par \par \uc2 The interbank market has effectively been frozen for three straight days after dollar supply all but dried up as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushes through the managed devaluation.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said Friday's dollar sales came too late in the day to kick-start trading and that banks had not been quoting any spreads throughout the day. Many banks bid unsuccessfully at below 130 to the dollar, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The Nigerian market will be closed on Monday and Tuesday for the Islamic holiday of Eid.\par \par \uc2 The regulator sold $180 million to one bank on Thursday at a rate of 128 to the dollar, considered too little to calm the market in the face of demand of around $2 billion.\par \par \uc2 It sold $180 million at its bi-weekly auction on Wednesday at 127-129 to the dollar compared to around 117 a week earlier.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Chukwuma Soludo told Reuters late on Wednesday that the regulator was willing to meet all demand for dollars at a market-determined exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 But the country's banks have appeared reluctant to buy dollars at the rates being offered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They are trying to protect themselves against a weaker naira in the medium-term by been shifting their balance sheets into dollars, further pushing up demand for the greenback and tightening the market, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts have said they believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have deliberately been restricting dollar supply to the market in order to flush out speculators and ascertain the true level of underlying demand.\par \par \uc2 Soludo said on Wednesday that those who had been speculating in the market would be "made to pay a heavy price". (Writing by Nick Tattersall; Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|G|AFN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|RNP|DNP|PGE|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081205e4c5001ca\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
