\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Nigeria's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  to act to stabilise naira\b0\par\par\uc2 By Oludare Mayowa   \par \uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2008\par 00:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds background)\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Dec 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from Thursday to ensure the naira's stability after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell sharply against the U.S. dollar, Governor Chukwuma Soludo said.\par \par \uc2 "We are ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, beginning from tomorrow (Thursday). The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will meet all demand at the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at the market-determined exchange rate," Soludo told Reuters by telephone.\par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ready to buy and sell as necessary.\par \par \uc2 The naira <NGN=> weakened close to 8 percent to almost 130 to the U.S. dollar on Tuesday as dealers digested the impact of a budget announcement by the president and reacted to what appeared to be a managed depreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Banks said no spreads were being quoted on Wednesday on the interbank market as dealers waited for clarity on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy and as dollar supply all but dried up.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed the naira, broadly stable against the dollar for months, to depreciate further at its biweekly auction on Wednesday, selling at between 127-129 compared to around 118 on Monday and 116 a week ago.\par \par \uc2 It sold only $180 million on Wednesday and $100 million on Monday despite demand of about $2 billion, leaving banks scrambling for dollars from other sources.\par \par \uc2 Soludo blamed the naira's depreciation on speculators.\par \par \uc2 "Those who have been speculating in the market will be made to pay a heavy price for their actions," he said.\par \par \uc2 HURT BY DROP IN OIL DEMAND\par \par \uc2 President Umaru Yar'Adua proposed a 2.87 trillion naira ($24 billion) 2009 budget on Tuesday, a slight increase over actual spending this year despite lower world oil prices, and sought approval to breach a budget deficit target of 3 percent.\par \par \uc2 That highlighted concern that Nigeria's fiscal position had been impaired significantly by lower world oil demand and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had decided to allow the naira to weaken.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said dollar demand was being driven by importers before the Christmas trading season as well as by portfolio investors who have been taking money out of Nigeria as the global credit crisis dampens appetite for risk.\par \par \uc2 It has also been fueled by banks, businesses and individuals -- worried by the long-term impact of falling oil prices on Nigeria's economy -- shifting their balance sheets out of naira into U.S. dollars.\par \par \uc2 One banking analyst said he thought the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have deliberately restricted dollar supply to the market in order to flush out speculators and ascertain the true level of underlying demand. (Writing by Nick Tattersall; Editing by Jan Paschal)\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|BNX|ABX|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|U|UKI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081203e4c300203\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
