\par\par \b \uc2 Nigerian naira slips vs dollar from 5-year high   \b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2007\par 18:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Oct 25 (Reuters) - The Nigerian naira weakened to 121.50 per dollar <NGN=>on the interbank market on Thursday from a 5-year high of 118.50 on Wednesday, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 Bankers said the market was drained of excess liquidity after investors made purchases at an auction of sovereign bonds on Thursday and importers took advantage of the naira rally to buy more dollars.   \par \par \uc2 "The initial appreciation of the naira was due to massive dollar sales by some banks that needed naira cash to invest in bonds on behalf of their customers," one dealer said. "Now that the auction is over, the gain is being reversed."   \par \par \uc2 Nigeria auctioned a total of 42.81 billion naira in 3-year and 10-year sovereign bonds at par with 7.0 percent and 9.35 percent coupon respectively on Thursday, the Debt Management Office said.   \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the naira climbed to its strongest level in five years on a surge in dollar inflows from off-shore interests and some oil multinationals.   \par \par \uc2 As a consequence of the naira's recent steady rally against the dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been forced to suspend its twice-weekly \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction to commercial banks and has indicated it could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the naira's rapid appreciation.   \par \par \uc2 Bankers predicted that the naira could remain stable at 121.50/122 per dollar in the weeks ahead on fears of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 NIGERIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -NAIRA/|LANGEN|AFN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PT