\par\par \b \uc2 Nigerian naira strengthens to 129.57/$ at auction  \b0\par\par\uc2 230 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2005\par 15:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Aug 30 (Reuters) - The Nigerian naira <NGN=> strengthened to 129.57 per dollar on Tuesday from 129.87 per dollar previously despite a surge in demand for dollars, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.  \par \par \uc2 Details of the twice-weekly auction released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed that demand for the dollar rose to $143.69 million from $46.01 million on Thursday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it sold $128.84 million to end-users through their banks, compared with $45.01 million previously.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the world's eighth largest oil exporter, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last Tuesday, offering $500 million in a special sale outside the twice-weekly auction system.  \par \par \uc2 The special auction, which was seen by industry official as preparatory to introducing a new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy next year, led to an appreciation in the value of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  across all segments of the market.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the naira also strengthened on the interbank market to 131.60 a dollar from 132.15, due to higher inflows from multinational oil firms, bankers said.  \par \par \uc2 Four oil companies sold about $70 million to selected banks between Thursday and Monday, dealers said. The naira remained unchanged on the black market, trading at 144 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-NIGERIA-NAIRA|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|AFN|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050830e18u0019u\par }\page {\