\par\par \b \uc2  Nigerian naira steady on  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1999\par 09:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LAGOS, Jan 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped stabilise \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's naira, but \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said on Friday there was a limit to how long foreign reserves could last given low oil export prices. \par \par \uc2  On the parallel market the dollar sold for 94 naira, the same level as last week and compared to 97 naira two weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  At the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weekly auction, demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 86 naira to the dollar rose to $97 million from $87 million last week - already more than the weekly amount budgeted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year. \par \par \uc2  "The long-term view is one of devaluation. The fundamental is still wrong," said one bank dealer, adding that if the military government kept to its spending plan before stepping down in May, the naira would come under greater pressure. \par \par \uc2  High \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand three weeks ago in anticipation of a devaluation fell back after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had budgeted $4.4 billion for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1999 and would defend the naira. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was wildly optimistic in its prediction of receipts from private sources of $2.5 billion to fund the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with a further $1.9 billion from government. \par \par \uc2  "The only alternative to devaluation is to use foreign reserves, which is politically popular but unwise in the long term if oil prices stay low," said one banker. \par \par \uc2  ((Paul Okolo, Lagos newsroom +234 1 2630317)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1t05heu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
