\par\par \b \uc2  Nigeria confident about IMF talks. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tunde Obadina \par \uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ABUJA, May 22 (Reuter) - Nigeria said on Monday it was confident about reaching agreement with the International Monetary Fund (IMF) on a policy package that it hopes will open the way for negotiations with creditors on debt relief. \par \par \uc2  The optimism was voiced by Nigerian Finance Minister Anthony Ani ahead of talks starting this week with an IMF team. \par \par \uc2  Ani told Reuters the government still aimed to reach an accord with the Fund and the World Bank on the government's package, called the Medium Term Economic Adjustment Programme, by the start of the third quarter of 1995. \par \par \uc2  "We are still very optimistic because we are on course." \par \par \uc2  In its 1995 budget Nigeria's military government announced measures that took the country back towards free market reforms after a year of turning away from IMF-backed policies started by a previous administration in 1986. \par \par \uc2  International finance agencies have commended some aspects of the 1995 budget, including the re-introduction of an autonomous \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the removal of laws that restricted foreign investment. \par \par \uc2  But they say the government needs to liberalise further. Among other things it should abolish the official exchange rate of 22 naira to the dollar, which compares to a current rate of about 83.50 naira to the dollar in the autonomous market. \par \par \uc2  They also oppose the retention of a 21 percent ceiling on interest rates and apparent moves to take over privatised banks. \par \par \uc2  Ani said the official exchange rate existed only for internal accounting purposes and that the effective rate in the economy was that of the autonomous market. \par \par \uc2  He said the government aimed for a unified rate and hoped to agree with the IMF on a timetable for achieving this. \par \par \uc2  "We are not going to have two rates for ever. We expect them to merge between now and the next 18 months," he said. \par \par \uc2  Ani said the government was looking at how to make the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  discount rate the focus of bank interest rates. He added that the government would not allow a return to the 1993 situation when interest rates topped 100 percent. \par \par \uc2  "We cannot allow a situation where banks move interest rates so that they adversely affect manufacturers and the economy." \par \par \uc2  Ani said the government was still committed to privatisation, which was begun in 1988 and suspended in January this year. \par \par \uc2  "We are not going back on the privatisation policies. Government is committed to privatisation," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said government plans to re-establish its presence in the country's four biggest banks, privatised between 1992 and 1993, did not involve re-nationalisation. \par \par \uc2  He said the decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the First Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Union Bank, the United Bank for Africa and Afribank was made to prevent them from being "hijacked". \par \par \uc2  He said the banks were too crucial to the economy for the government to allow them to be taken over by people who might run them into the ground. \par \par \uc2  Ani said the government's Medium Term Economic Adjustment Programme was an update of a 1993 that was not implemented. \par \par \uc2  That three-year programme was was geared to achieving a 5.3 percent GDP annual growth rate, cutting inflation to five percent and reducing the fiscal deficit as a percentage of GDP to 3.3 percent. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr5m07i3v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
