\par\par \b \uc2  Nigeria  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  cautious on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  policy. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tunde Obadina \par \uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LAGOS, Feb 16 (Reuter) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CBN) will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's newly legalised autonomous \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market until banks raise their quotes for official funds, the bank's spokesman said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The days of cheap \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  are over. There is no more subsidised \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," CBN spokesman Tony Ede told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  He said daily exchange rates quoted by banks to the CBN have not so far reflected the state of the market. \par \par \uc2  "The rates they are quoting for the dollar are too low. They are not the same rates as we know the banks are actually selling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,"  he said. \par \par \uc2  He did not say what rates banks have quoted the CBN. \par \par \uc2  Banks on Thursday quoted to the public a dollar selling rate of between 78 and 82 naira. \par \par \uc2  The dollar sold for about 105 naira in November before falling partly on anticipation of the announcment of the 1995 government budget. \par \par \uc2  The government, under pressure from local private sector groups and foreign creditors, in mid-January legalised the autonomous market after a year of imposing an officially set and highly subsidised fixed exchange rate regime. \par \par \uc2  Paul Ogwuma, CBN governor, said at a luncheon on Thursday Nigeria had become over-dependent on imported raw materials and finished goods. \par \par \uc2  "This largely stems from the past misalignment of the naira exchange rate - which subsidised the consumption of foreign goods and services to the disadvantage of domestic production. \par \par \uc2  "We are indeed hopeful that the new exchange rate policy, if sustained, shall compel the economy to look inwards for a change," he said. \par \par \uc2  The CBN has stopped its fortnightly \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales to the public, saying it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it deems it necessary. \par \par \uc2  The autonomous market has not fully taken off partly because banks and their clients are waiting for the CBN to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and inject scarce hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the system. \par \par \uc2  Many people believe the CBN will inject money into the system at rates below those of the free market. \par \par \uc2  It appears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also waiting for the market to come to terms with a CBN that seems committed to promoting free market forces after years of artificially propping up the naira. \par \par \uc2  "We are waiting for them to understand the system. The market has not come to grips yet with the current reality. We are not getting the right signals," Ede said. \par \par \uc2  Under the new system the CBN when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  will sell \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to end users through selected banks. \par \par \uc2  Managers at Nigeria's 116 commercial and merchant banks have been anxious to know what criteria the CBN will use to select the banks. \par \par \uc2  With the CBN controlling the bulk of the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is likely to be traded in the autonomous market, no bank wants to be left out of its list. \par \par \uc2  Ede said banks able to buy and sell at the highest rates stood the best chance. \par \par \uc2  "We know the active banks in the market. We will look at their rates and sell through them to end users at the highest rates quoted by these banks," he said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr2g01427\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
