\par\par \b \uc2  Nigerian banks to sell  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  directly to end users. \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LAGOS, Feb 10 (Reuter) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Nigeria (CBN) said it will sell hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to end users when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the newly legalised autonomous \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  It said in guidelines on the liberalised \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market announced by the government last month that it would sell funds to end users through selected banks who may charge transaction charges and commission but not a spread. \par \par \uc2  The guidelines did not say what criteria would be used to select the banks. \par \par \uc2  Nigeria's 116 commercial and merchant banks have anxiously waited for the CBN to spell out how it planned to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the autonomous market. \par \par \uc2  The CBN said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shall be "when considered necessary giving only short notice of such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2  shall sell \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the current autonomous selling rate in the market," it said. \par \par \uc2  The CBN earlier this week issued and later withdrew guidelines which said it would sell \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the highest interbank rates. \par \par \uc2  Friday's guidelines said banks must submit to CBN summaries of their client's applications for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  within 48 hours from the time of notification of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the CBN. \par \par \uc2  --Lagos newsroom +234 1 2630317 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr2a019rm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
