\par\par \b \uc2  Nigeria aims to make naira convertible  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LAGOS, Jan 24 (Reuter) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Nigeria (CBN) said it was working towards making the naira a convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The major policy goal for 1995 is the deliberate build-up and strengthening of external reserves to enhance confidence in the Nigerian economy, strengthen the naira and pave the way for its ultimate convertibility," CBN governor Paul Ogwuma told a rare news conference in Lagos. \par \par \uc2  Nigeria's external reserves last July stood at $669 million, barely enough to pay for six weeks worth of imports. The government on January 14 legalised the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in a move back to free market reforms abandoned a year ago. \par \par \uc2  Ogwuma said the government's 1994 policy of fixing the exchange rate at 22 naira to the dollar, a fraction of rates in the parallel market, had not worked. \par \par \uc2  "In the area of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  management, lessons of experience have clearly shown that the regime of fixed exchange rates that was pursued in 1994 did not achieve the intended policy objectives," he said. \par \par \uc2  The government fixed the exchange rate in a bid to strengthen the naira which in 1985 was worth more than a dollar. \par \par \uc2  Under the new system the interbank market is free to operate rates mutually agreed between buyers and sellers. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stopped its fortnightly \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales and says it will instead \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  periodically in the autonomous market by selling and buying \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at market rates. \par \par \uc2  There has been few transactions in the autonomous market as banks wait for the CBN to sell them scarce hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings, mainly from crude oil exports, account for the bulk of \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflow. \par \par \uc2  Ogwuma said the CBN would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the autonomous market having conducted a survey of banks' buying and selling rates as well as their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  requirements. The CBN did not expect demand for its hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be as high as it was last year when it sold funds at highly subsidised official rates. \par \par \uc2  The increased cost of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will force importers to seek local substitutes for imported production inputs, he said. \par \par \uc2  "The demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  is well within our means to meet," he said. "Most of the people who demanded dollars last year are going to be looking inwards this year," he said. \par \par \uc2  The government still maintains an official exchange rate of 22 naira to the dollar, but that rate applies to a limited number of government transactions. \par \par \uc2  All individuals, private sector operators and government parastatals run on commercial basis must buy their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the autonomous market where the dollar now sells at well above 70 naira. \par \par \uc2  Bankers say the two-tier \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system is open to abuse as officials with access to subsidised hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be tempted to divert to to the autonomous market. \par \par \uc2  Ogwuma said the government would take steps to prevent the occurance of this practice reputed to have made some well placed people rich in the past. \par \par \uc2  "What the government is going to do is to ensure there is no round-tripping," he said. \par \par \uc2  --Lagos newsroom +234 1 2630317 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr1o04bj0\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (nigeria near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdr